script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'adr123-review-and-scout',
  description: 'Adversarially check the ADR-123 sondeo claims and scout the junk-guard refutation',
  phases: [{ title: 'Review' }, { title: 'Scout' }],
}

const RULES = `Context: Lean 4 repo at E:\\dropbox\\github\\lean4\\ROBINSON_PlusPlus (RPP), sibling FOL at E:\\dropbox\\github\\lean4\\FOL.
HARD RULES: never run lake, lean, elan, leanchecker (not in Windows, not in WSL). Read-only: do not edit, create, or delete any file in either repo.
Use Grep/Read/Glob (or read-only shell: grep, sed -n, cat). Answer in English, concisely, with file:line references.`

const SONDEO = `The new sondeo is sondeos/RosserReflexion.lean (180 lines). It proves, via reflection (internal evaluation pcc_eval_substfc_wit / pcc_eval_liftfc_wit + soundness prf_sound in the standard model MNV V₀ + W1 verificador_solido + the decoder dec/decT), that for numerals with guards TRUE in the model:
  Prf (Formula.eq (substfc (numeralM a) (numeralM b) (numeralM c)) (numeralM (substfcN a b c)))   [prf_eval_substfc_num, hyps hasWitN b, hasWitFN c]
  Prf (Formula.eq (liftfc (numeralM a) (numeralM c)) (numeralM (liftfcN a c)))                    [prf_eval_liftfc_num, hyp hasWitFN c]
plus no-vacuity corollaries over real codes (hasWitN_codigo, hasWitFN_codigo, prf_eval_substfc_codigo, dec_valor_substfc, ...).
ADR-123 is appended at the end of DECISIONS.md.`

phase('Review')
const review = parallel([
  () => agent(`${RULES}\n\n${SONDEO}\n\nTASK (duplicates — the repo rule is "before building, SEARCH"): for EACH theorem declared in sondeos/RosserReflexion.lean (ev_numeral, ev_strCode, ev_liftfc, ev_uno, ev_cuatro, ev_evalSubstfcCode, ev_eqcLiftfc, decT_tcFnN, ev_provFromCode, prf_dec_of_prov, prf_eval_substfc_num, prf_eval_liftfc_num, hasWitN_codigo, hasWitFN_codigo, prf_eval_substfc_codigo, dec_valor_substfc, prf_eval_liftfc_codigo, dec_valor_liftfc), search ROBINSON_PlusPlus/ (the build tree) and sondeos/ for an existing lemma with the SAME statement (possibly under another name or in another namespace; e.g. an existing evalTerm lemma for liftfc in Meta/ModeloCodificacion.lean, or an existing evaluation of Meta.Godel.numeral / Provability.strCode in the model, or a decoder lemma about tcFnN). Report each duplicate found with its location and exact statement, and say explicitly which ones have NO existing equivalent. Do not speculate: quote statements.`, { label: 'review:duplicates', phase: 'Review' }),
  () => agent(`${RULES}\n\n${SONDEO}\n\nTASK (adversarial reading): read sondeos/RosserReflexion.lean entirely and the ADR-123 section at the end of DECISIONS.md, and the new row for RosserReflexion.lean in sondeos/README.md, and item 1 of the list at the top of NEXT-STEPS.md. Try to REFUTE each claim made in that prose: (1) "sin inducción sobre la fórmula y sin tocar a mano un axioma de codificación"; (2) "No pide Prf guarda: basta que la guarda sea verdadera en el modelo"; (3) the no-vacuity claim (do hasWitN_codigo/hasWitFN_codigo really discharge the hypotheses for real codes; is prf_eval_substfc_codigo hypothesis-free); (4) "hoy ningún lema refuta una guarda (0 apariciones de 'neg (hasWit' en Meta/)" — grep for every form that would refute a guard: neg (hasWit, neg (hasWitF, impl (hasWit ...) bottom, Formula.impl (hasWit, ¬-forms in PrfH contexts; (5) the line figures (180 lines, 18 theorems, ~110 proof lines); (6) whether the statement direction/argument order of substfc and liftfc matches the model's interpretation (MNV in ROBINSON_PlusPlus/Meta/ModeloEstandar.lean: "substfc", [v, t, f] => substfcN v t f; "liftfc", [c, f] => liftfcN c f) and the internal evaluation's guards (hasWit on the 2nd argument, hasWitF on the 3rd). Return a list: claim → verdict (holds / refuted / imprecise) with evidence, and a suggested exact rewording for anything refuted or imprecise.`, { label: 'review:adversarial', phase: 'Review' }),
])

phase('Scout')
const scout = parallel([
  () => agent(`${RULES}\n\nTASK (scouting for the next proof, the "junk half" of NegNum in Rosser): we want to prove in the Hilbert calculus Prf (ROBINSON_PlusPlus/Meta/Hilbert.lean) the REFUTATION of a guard on a junk numeral, first at depth 0: Prf (neg (hasWit (numeralM 0))) — hasWit is defined in ROBINSON_PlusPlus/Minimal/Axioms.lean (around lines 1196-1277: hasWit, isTC1, wfAll1, wfAll1Body, isTermCodeE1, shapeUn, shapeBin, argsIn). Find and report, with exact statements and file:line:
 (a) the exact definitions of hasWit, isTC1, wfAll1, wfAll1Body, isTermCodeE1, shapeUn, shapeBin, argsIn, argsInBody, In, lenc, nthc;
 (b) any Prf/PrfH lemma converting membership into an index: In x L → ∃ i, lt i (lenc L) ∧ nthc L i = x (the converse of prf_in_nthc at ROBINSON_PlusPlus/Meta/SubstfcWitnessPrf.lean:549), or any "membership form" of wfAll1 (∀x. In x w → isTermCodeE1 w x);
 (c) any Prf lemma that cons a b ≠ zero (or σ t ≠ 0, Q1), i.e. Prf (neg (cons a b =eq zero)) or similar, and any lemma refuting numeral equalities (numeralM m =eq numeralM n for m ≠ n);
 (d) the PrfH elimination toolkit names for ∃ (PrfH_ex_elim), ∧, ∨ (or-elim), deduction (prf_deduction), and how a neg goal is usually closed in this codebase (look at a few existing proofs of Prf (neg ...)).
Return a compact report organised (a)-(d).`, { label: 'scout:junk-guard', phase: 'Scout' }),
])

const [r, s] = await Promise.all([review, scout])
return { review: r, scout: s }
